                <pb facs="0669" n="551" xml:id="pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/6177: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Eberhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-15T12:00:00-05:00">January 15,
                        1929—noon</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Your 17, January 9, 2 p.m. It is the feeling of the Department that this is a
                    matter in which the decision and responsibility should rest with the Government
                    of Nicaragua alone. If martial law is established, it should be carried out by
                    the authorities of Nicaragua only.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
